# sid:1 and sid:2 have two dependencies in the same direction: sid:1 sets x
# (read by sid:2) and sid:1 unsets y (read by sid:2 as isnotset). Those are two
# parallel graph edges between the same pair of signatures, with differing
# weights (set vs unset).
#
# The pair is also a genuine deadlock: sid:1 needs z, only set by sid:2, and
# sid:2 needs x, only set by sid:1. Neither can match first, so no order
# exists and the cycle must be reported rather than silently resolved.
alert tcp any any -> any any (flowbits:isset,z; flowbits:set,x; flowbits:unset,y; sid:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any any (flowbits:isset,x; flowbits:isnotset,y; flowbits:set,z; sid:2;)
